<%# ▲▼ — the give-way order without JavaScript. Locals: `group`, `groups`.

    TWO PLAIN FORMS, not two Stimulus actions, and that is the point of them: each button already
    carries the whole order as hidden `category_ids[]` fields, so the reorder works with scripting
    off and is testable without synthesising drag events. reorder_controller does the same thing
    from the DOM when a card is dropped; both submit one shape to one endpoint.

    Named, not just glyphed: `Capybara.enable_aria_label` is on, and "Move Groceries up" is also
    what a screen reader has to hear — a button whose only text is ▲ says nothing about what
    moves or where.

    THE LIST BAKED IN HERE IS AS OLD AS THE PAGE, and that is the accepted cost of the two
    builders: a button pressed after a rule was added or deleted in another tab submits a set
    that is no longer the user's `in_fill_order.with_a_rule` set, and `Category.apply_fill_order`
    refuses it whole. The stale press writes nothing and says to reload, which is the same answer
    a stale drag gets — no half-order is reachable from either. %>
<%# THE TARGET IS 44px SQUARE AND THE DISABLED STATE IS VISIBLE (design review M4).

    It was `px-1 text-xs` — a control roughly 18×16, which is under half the 44px minimum and sits
    a few pixels from its twin, on the one screen in this app that asks a user to press the same
    button repeatedly. The glyph stays small; the BOX grew, which is the whole fix.

    DISABLED WAS `text-gray-200` ON WHITE — 1.2:1, invisible. A disabled control still has to be
    findable: a user who cannot see the top card's ▲ cannot tell "already first" from "the arrows
    stopped working". Grey-500 on a grey-100 fill is 4.2:1, and the FILL rather than a paler glyph
    is what tells it apart from the enabled state, so neither reading depends on colour alone. %>
<span class="flex items-center gap-1 shrink-0">
  <% { -1 => ["▲", "up"], 1 => ["▼", "down"] }.each do |offset, (glyph, direction)| %>
    <%= button_to glyph,
                  budget_page_reorder_path,
                  method: :patch,
                  params: { category_ids: reordered_category_ids(groups, group, offset) },
                  disabled: reorder_edge?(groups, group, offset),
                  form_class: "inline-block leading-none",
                  aria: { label: "Move #{group.category.name} #{direction}" },
                  title: "Move #{group.category.name} #{direction}",
                  class: "inline-flex h-11 w-11 items-center justify-center text-xs rounded " \
                         "border border-gray-200 text-gray-700 transition-colors " \
                         "enabled:hover:text-gray-900 enabled:hover:border-gray-400 " \
                         "disabled:bg-gray-100 disabled:text-gray-500 disabled:border-gray-200" %>
  <% end %>
</span>
